{
  "title": "Cimmeria — Launcher journey",
  "description": "What the desktop launcher's attempt summaries (schema version 1) say about install, runtime setup, repair, uninstall and launch attempts. Cohort: attempts from opted-in launchers whose summary the server successfully received, and nothing else. This is not an all-player funnel, not an install success rate, and not a login or world-entry metric: a launch counts as succeeded when the observed game process exited with code 0. A launch row times only its preparation (the starting phase); the length of the play session is never reported. unknown is its own outcome (the launcher lost sight of the attempt); it is never folded into succeeded or failed. The rows are self-reported and can be forged within the ingest quota, so do not alert on them or set a target from them. Every panel is count() over launcher.summary rows in the cimmeria-client index. Attempt panels count event = launcher_summary and the phase panel counts event = launcher_phase, so an attempt is never counted once per timed phase. Reference: docs/operations/signoz/launcher-summary-views.md.",
  "tags": [
    "cimmeria",
    "launcher",
    "launcher-summary"
  ],
